What is the output of the following Java program featuring a static factory method?
```java
interface Notifier {
    void send(String msg);
}
class EmailNotifier implements Notifier {
    public void send(String msg) { System.out.print("Email:" + msg + " "); }
}
class SmsNotifier implements Notifier {
    public void send(String msg) { System.out.print("SMS:" + msg + " "); }
}
class NotifierFactory {
    public static Notifier create(String type) {
        if ("sms".equalsIgnoreCase(type)) return new SmsNotifier();
        return new EmailNotifier();
    }
}
public class FactoryApp {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Notifier n = NotifierFactory.create("sms");
        n.send("Alert");
    }
}
```

What is the output of the following Java program implementing the Strategy pattern?
```java
interface DiscountStrategy {
    double apply(double total);
}
class FlatDiscount implements DiscountStrategy {
    public double apply(double total) { return total - 10.0; }
}
class PercentDiscount implements DiscountStrategy {
    public double apply(double total) { return total * 0.80; }
}
class OrderContext {
    private DiscountStrategy strategy;
    public OrderContext(DiscountStrategy s) { this.strategy = s; }
    public void setStrategy(DiscountStrategy s) { this.strategy = s; }
    public double compute(double amt) { return strategy.apply(amt); }
}
public class StrategyApp {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        OrderContext ctx = new OrderContext(new FlatDiscount());
        System.out.print((int) ctx.compute(100.0) + " ");
        ctx.setStrategy(new PercentDiscount());
        System.out.print((int) ctx.compute(100.0));
    }
}
```

